 "note": "For each verifier line, uid is joined to the main example. gold is the writer's label (ANLI field 'label'); verifier labels are 2 (or 3 when the first 2 disagreed) independent checks. strict majority = a label held by more than half the verifier votes (a 1-1 pair or a 1-1-1 triple has none). n_gold_matches_majority / n_gold_differs_from_majority / n_no_majority partition the joined dev/test examples with a recognised gold. n_unanimous_differs_from_gold counts the striking case where every verifier agreed with each other but none agreed with the writer's gold. P1 bets verification is dev/test only (no verifier uid maps to a train example); P2 bets every verifier line carries 2 or 3 labels; P3 bets -- unlike the majority-defined SNLI/MultiNLI gold -- ANLI's gold differs from the verifier majority on a nonzero number of rows. The exact agreement rate is reported, not pre-bet on a guessed number; orphan verifier uids (no main example) are reported, not bet on."
